 "_gim_web": "GIM6010-36 and GIM8115-9 come from the parameter image on their steadywin-motor.com listings (the 48 V driver column; weight is with the driver fitted). GIM8115-36 and WGG7210-12.5 publish no parameter table at all — theirs stay blank rather than interpolated from the 9:1 model.",
 "_wgg": "The WGG exoskeleton family comes from WGG外骨骼电机选型表2026.02.13.xlsx, the factory selection table — steadywin-motor.com shows an empty parameter block for these. Weight is the motor without its driver, which is the only figure that sheet publishes (the GIM rows elsewhere are with the driver fitted). The sheet names the 12.5:1 model WGG7010-12.5; the shop calls it WGG7210-12.5, and Ø73.2 fits the shop's number, so that is the one kept."
